{"course": {"id": "s16", "title": "Camday – Cambridge Primary Mathematics — Stage 6", "units": [{"n": 1, "t": "The Number System"}, {"n": 2, "t": "Numbers and Sequences"}, {"n": 3, "t": "Averages"}, {"n": 4, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (1)"}, {"n": 5, "t": "2D Shapes"}, {"n": 6, "t": "Fractions and Percentages"}, {"n": 7, "t": "Exploring Measures"}, {"n": 8, "t": "Addition and Subtraction (2)"}, {"n": 9, "t": "Probability"}, {"n": 10, "t": "Multiplication and Division (1)"}, {"n": 11, "t": "3D Shapes"}, {"n": 12, "t": "Ratio and Proportion"}, {"n": 13, "t": "Angles"}, {"n": 14, "t": "Multiplication and Division (2)"}, {"n": 15, "t": "Data"}, {"n": 16, "t": "The Laws of Arithmetic"}, {"n": 17, "t": "Transformations"}]}, "unit": {"n": 6, "stage": 16, "title": "Fractions and Percentages", "strandShort": "Number", "blurb": "Fractions as division, finding fractions of amounts, percentages of shapes and amounts, and comparing fractions, decimals and percentages.", "strand": "Number", "framework": "Cambridge Primary Mathematics (0096), Stage 6", "lesson": true, "subject": "maths", "read": "media/read/m6u06.pdf"}, "objectives": {"O1": {"code": "6Nf.01", "sec": "6.1", "codeNote": "", "t": "Understand that a fraction can be a division (3/4 = 3 ÷ 4), and find fractions of quantities."}, "O2": {"code": "6Nf.02", "sec": "6.2", "codeNote": "", "t": "Understand percentages as parts of 100 and find simple percentages of quantities."}, "O3": {"code": "6Nf.03", "sec": "6.3", "codeNote": "", "t": "Recognise equivalent fractions, decimals and percentages, and compare and order them."}}, "sections": [{"id": "6.1", "title": "Understanding fractions", "objs": ["O1"], "lesson": [{"k": "hook", "t": "Sharing pizzas", "p": ["**3 pizzas** are shared equally between **4 friends**.", "How much pizza does each friend get? Is it more or less than a whole pizza? Try it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Fractions", "p": ["¾ means 3 parts out of 4 equal parts."], "qq": {"id": "m6u06s1t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "What fraction of a pizza is 1 slice if it is cut into 8 equal slices? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.125, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "1/8."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "A fraction is a division", "p": ["**3 ÷ 4 = ¾**: each friend gets ¾ of a pizza. The **numerator** is divided by the **denominator**.", "Improper fractions work the same way: **7 ÷ 2 = 7/2 = 3½**."], "table": {"head": ["Division", "Fraction", "Mixed number"], "rows": [["3 ÷ 4", "3/4", "–"], ["7 ÷ 2", "7/2", "3½"], ["11 ÷ 3", "11/3", "3⅔"], ["5 ÷ 5", "5/5", "1"]]}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Fractions as operators", "p": ["'Find ⅗ **of** 40' means divide by 5, then multiply by 3: 40 ÷ 5 = 8, 8 × 3 = **24**.", "Improper fractions can be operators too: 5/4 of 20 = 20 ÷ 4 × 5 = **25** – more than 20!"]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Of", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u06s1t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Find ⅔ of 27.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 18, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "27 ÷ 3 × 2.", "reason": "18."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I use fractions?", "p": ["Step 1: A fraction a/b means a ÷ b.", "Step 2: To find a fraction of an amount: divide by the denominator.", "Step 3: Then multiply by the numerator.", "Step 4: Improper fractions give more than the original amount."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Division as a fraction", "p": [], "q": "Share 5 cakes between 3 people.", "steps": [["5 ÷ 3 = 5/3", ""], ["= 1⅔", ""]], "a": "1⅔ cakes each"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Of an amount", "p": [], "q": "Find ⅞ of 56.", "steps": [["56 ÷ 8 = 7", ""], ["7 × 7 = 49", ""]], "a": "49"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Improper operator", "p": [], "q": "Find 3/2 of 18.", "steps": [["18 ÷ 2 = 9", ""], ["9 × 3 = 27", ""]], "a": "27"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Units", "p": [], "q": "Find ¾ of 2 m in cm.", "steps": [["2 m = 200 cm", ""], ["200 ÷ 4 × 3 = 150", ""]], "a": "150 cm"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Division", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u06s1t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "9 ÷ 4 as a mixed number?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "2¼", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "4/9", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Divided by the numerator", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Find ⅖ of 30.", "lines": ["30 ÷ 2 = 15", "15 × 5 = 75"], "bad": 0, "why": "Divide by the DENOMINATOR (5) then multiply by the numerator (2): 30 ÷ 5 × 2 = 12.", "fix": [["30 ÷ 5 = 6", ""], ["6 × 2 = 12", ""]], "id": "m6u06s1t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Dividing by the top number", "p": ["Divide by the bottom, multiply by the top."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Sharing food, splitting bills and recipes all use fractions as division and as operators."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["a/b = a ÷ b.", "Fraction of an amount: ÷ denominator, × numerator.", "Improper fractions are more than 1 whole.", "Change mixed and improper fractions as needed."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 720, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "6.1-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u06s1k01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Before you read on: pizza each? Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.75, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": ""}}, {"id": "6.1-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u06s1k02", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "11 ÷ 3 = ?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "3⅔", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "3⅓", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "6.1-k3", "t": 3, "after": 9, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u06s1k03", "type": "num", "prompt": "⅗ of 40?", "diff":