s", "p": ["Ella scored **18/25** in a spelling test, Finn got **0.7** of his questions right, and Gia scored **68%**.", "Who did best? How can you compare numbers written in different ways? Think about it before you read on."]}, {"k": "recall", "t": "Equivalent fractions", "p": ["½ = 2/4 = 5/10 = 50/100."], "qq": {"id": "m6u06s3t01", "type": "num", "prompt": "Write 6/8 in its simplest form. Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 0.75, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 1e-06, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "", "reason": "3/4."}}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Simplest form", "p": ["Divide the numerator and denominator by their **highest common factor**: 18/24 → ÷ 6 → **3/4**.", "A fraction is in its simplest form when no number except 1 divides both."]}, {"k": "idea", "t": "Fractions, decimals and percentages", "p": ["Change everything to the **same form** to compare (percentages are often easiest)."], "table": {"head": ["Fraction", "Decimal", "Percentage"], "rows": [["1/2", "0.5", "50%"], ["1/4", "0.25", "25%"], ["3/4", "0.75", "75%"], ["1/5", "0.2", "20%"], ["1/10", "0.1", "10%"], ["18/25 = 72/100", "0.72", "72%"]]}, "p2": ["Ella 72%, Finn 70%, Gia 68% → **Ella** did best."]}, {"k": "try", "t": "Percent", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u06s3t02", "type": "num", "prompt": "Write 3/5 as a percentage.", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Application", "answer": 60, "unit": "×", "units": ["×"], "tol": 0, "errs": [], "bare": true, "hint": "3/5 = 60/100.", "reason": "60."}}, {"k": "method", "t": "How do I compare fractions, decimals and percentages?", "p": ["Step 1: Change each to a percentage (or a decimal).", "Step 2: Fractions: make the denominator 100 if you can (e.g. ×4 for 25ths).", "Step 3: Decimals: × 100 for a percentage.", "Step 4: Compare and order."]}, {"k": "example", "t": "Simplify", "p": [], "q": "Simplify 15/40.", "steps": [["HCF 5", ""], ["3/8", ""]], "a": "3/8"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Decimal to percentage", "p": [], "q": "0.35 as a percentage and fraction.", "steps": [["35%", ""], ["35/100 = 7/20", ""]], "a": "35% = 7/20"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Order", "p": [], "q": "Order 2/5, 0.38, 41%.", "steps": [["40%, 38%, 41%", ""]], "a": "0.38, 2/5, 41%"}, {"k": "example", "t": "Not out of 100", "p": [], "q": "Which is bigger: 7/20 or 0.4?", "steps": [["7/20 = 35/100 = 35%", ""], ["0.4 = 40%", ""]], "a": "0.4"}, {"k": "try", "t": "Order", "p": [], "qq": {"id": "m6u06s3t03", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Largest?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "0.8", "ok": true, "fb": "80%."}, {"t": "3/4", "ok": false, "fb": "75%."}, {"t": "78%", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"k": "error", "t": "Compared numerators", "p": ["Find the first wrong line."], "q": "Which is bigger, 3/5 or 4/10?", "lines": ["4 > 3, so 4/10 is bigger"], "bad": 0, "why": "Compare equal-sized parts: 3/5 = 6/10 > 4/10, so 3/5 is bigger.", "fix": [["3/5 = 6/10", ""], ["6/10 > 4/10", ""]], "id": "m6u06s3t04"}, {"k": "mistake", "t": "Comparing tops of fractions with different bottoms", "p": ["Make the denominators the same (or use %)."]}, {"k": "tip", "t": "Real life", "p": ["Test scores, survey results and battery levels are compared by converting to percentages."]}, {"k": "summary", "t": "What to remember", "p": ["Simplify using the HCF.", "Know ½, ¼, ¾, ⅕, ⅒ as decimals and %.", "Convert to the same form to compare.", "Equal denominators → compare numerators."]}], "video": {"src": null, "offset": 0, "dur": 660, "range": ""}, "stops": [{"id": "6.3-k1", "t": 1, "after": 0, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u06s3k01", "type": "mcq", "prompt": "Before you read on: who did best?", "diff": "M", "obj": "O1", "skill": "Reasoning", "hint": "", "reason": "", "options": [{"t": "Ella (72%)", "ok": true, "fb": ""}, {"t": "Finn", "ok": false, "fb": ""}]}}, {"id": "6.3-k2", "t": 2, "after": 4, "review": [0, 0], "note": "", "q": {"id": "m6u06s3k02"